The chain it keeps: she is identified through exactly three followers → she comes to the plank
without an opening speech → she presents the slip → only then Pike reads. The plan requires only
that a woman captain's line is read before and after. Break it: enter on Pike's first spoken version
or on the disputed lame mule; let it come out that the other three are hers only after the witness
is checked; let the slip arrive by another hand or already lie under Pike's stone. A reworded
sentence that keeps those links in that order still tracks.

