## 4. Standing defaults

**PASS.** Across all seven chapters there are no English weekday names, calendar month names or named seasons; “Fifth-day” is the academy's established house term, while “season's open,” “snow,” “frost” and “thaw” are work/weather descriptions rather than a named calendar season (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:39`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:227-237`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:307,353`). There are no metric units: distances use feet, yards, miles, paces and strides (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:73,103,143`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:183-185,239-257`). No elapsed year count since Kindling is given; the prose uses only unnumbered “since my Kindling” (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:233`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:287`). Cael says eighteen and never hints at nineteen (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:205-207`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:217`). “His Path” at `manuscript/chapter-06.md:121` belongs to Seln, not Cael; Cael is consistently given fragments, no Path, tier or rank (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:29-35`; `manuscript/chapter-07.md:287`). The violence, bodily cost and language remain within Reader Standard throughout `manuscript/chapter-01.md:1-367` through `manuscript/chapter-07.md:1-383`.

