## 2. The movement plan

**Beat order — PASS.** The shelf, days 4-6 skip, courier, three carts and road etiquette occur first (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:3-365`); Lowmarch and the board follow on day 9 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:9-281`); sale/reserve and the ferry escort follow in the first week (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:3-309`); the hold, fence and wash follow (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:3-105,157-243,285-353`); the Thornwater road and five observations follow (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:3-257`); Thornwater, the six-day stay, copied line and day-46 log follow (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:3-237`); and the day-49 board anatomy, wall, first pole and silent Teague/Cael reading close the movement (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:3-383`). No packet beat is missing or transposed.

