editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-33.md:173:Brom told her, and she listened. Then she came in, and sat on the floor with her back to the wall, and drew a line on her sheet at the bell, and wrote beside it, in her wide crooked left-handed letters, *Doorway. Uncommanded. Twelve seconds. Brom counting.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-33.md:179:He stood in the doorway with his hands in his coat pockets and did not come in. He looked at Lira's foot on the stool and at Brom's sling and at the strapping round Cael's ribs where his shirt was open, and at the rota nailed to the inside of the door. He read the rota. Cael watched him read it, all of it, down to *SOMEBODY IN THE ROOM. ALWAYS.*, and then look at the doorway he was standing in, as if it had told him something he did not have words for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-33.md:209:"The leaf. I sat at the sill with all of you on the Second-day and priced it. I wrote down everything I could think of, the first minute and a week without the band and the lane and the read and somebody in the room. I left blanks where I didn't know, the way Seln said." He looked at the door. "There wasn't a line for that. There wasn't a line that said it might do something on its own, in a doorway, to Lira, with me lying here saying *no*. I didn't think of it. I measured it wrong."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-33.md:227:"You sat at that sill on the Second-day with the rain on the window and measured it cold," said Brom. "Three times. With all of us. You wrote down what you could see and left blanks where you couldn't. Then it went in the fire, on a road, and it did something in a doorway that nobody could have measured, because nobody's ever had this iron before." He opened his eyes at last and looked at Cael across the dark room. "You've measured. That's the part that's yours."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-33.md:229:"And the doorway?" said Cael at last.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-33.md:231:"The doorway's the fire's," said Brom. "We'll write it down. Next time there's a leaf, it'll have a line for doorways." He shut his eyes again. "Go to sleep. I'm counting."
