editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-13.md:85:"The gallery," said Brom, from the doorway. "Who comes."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-13.md:97:He was young, younger than any registry officer Cael had seen in a doorway, and he had a heavy cold. He held a folded handkerchief in the hand that was not holding the board, and between names he turned his head politely away and used it, and turned back, and found his place on the board with one finger. He did not apologize for the cold or for the door or for the people on the steps. He read the list.
